        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(restart): keep deferring when pending inspection fails",
        "body": "Fixes #104064.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nGateway restart deferral treated pending-work inspection exceptions as proof that the gateway was idle. That fail-open path could restart while active work still existed but could not be inspected. The first patch fixed the helper retry behavior, but the config-reload caller still cleared its restartPending guard from onCheckError even though the helper now keeps polling. A later config change could therefore start duplicate deferral loops and competing restart preparation.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Treat pending-count inspection exceptions as unknown pending work instead of safe-to-restart.\n- Keep the existing deferral lifecycle active after both initial and later getPendingCount failures.\n- Preserve the config-reload restartPending guard when retrying inspection failures.\n- Update the production warning to say the deferral is waiting and retrying instead of restarting immediately.\n- Continue polling until a later check confirms idle, or until the explicit maxWaitMs timeout forces the existing timeout path.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact-head validation on 422023a5d715b3833c1683df674ae6b57662e4a7:\n\n- node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/restart.deferral-timeout.test.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.test.ts -> passed; 2 shards, 107 tests.\n- node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.non-agents.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-test-non-agents.tsbuildinfo -> passed.\n- ./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/infra/restart.ts src/infra/restart.deferral-timeout.test.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.test.ts -> passed.\n- ./node_modules/.bin/oxlint src/infra/restart.ts src/infra/restart.deferral-timeout.test.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.test.ts -> passed.\n- pnpm check:loc --base upstream/main --head HEAD -> passed.\n- git diff --check -> passed.\n\nFocused behavior covered:\n\n- Initial pending inspection throw calls onCheckError, enters deferral with pending=1, and later emits only after a successful idle check.\n- Later polling throw calls onCheckError, keeps polling, and later emits only after a successful idle check.\n- Config-reload caller keeps restartPending active after an inspection error; a later config restart request does not create duplicate restart emission work.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe helper and its production caller disagreed about onCheckError semantics. The helper now treats inspection failure as non-terminal, so the caller must keep its deferral guard active until ready, timeout, cancel, or emission settlement.\n\n## Behavior After This Patch\n\n- Initial inspection throw: calls onCheckError, enters deferral with pending=1, and polls again.\n- Later polling throw: calls onCheckError, keeps the interval registered, and retries on the next poll.\n- Config reload inspection throw: keeps restartPending true and logs waiting/retrying.\n- Confirmed pending=0 still emits restart through the normal ready path.\n- Explicit maxWaitMs still preserves the existing forced-timeout behavior.",
